From: e2631 tree fork <e2631@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] libfstools: skip the jffs2 overlay sync when there is no upper

jffs2_switch() calls switch2jffs(), which mounts the jffs2 volume at
/tmp/root, and then copies its upper/ directory back onto the root file
system.  A first boot with a RAM overlay has a fresh jffs2 volume with no
/tmp/root/upper yet, so "cp -a /tmp/root/upper/* /" matched nothing,
busybox reported the glob failure and fstools logged

    failed to sync jffs2 overlay

on every such boot, even though there was nothing to synchronize.  Under
the e2631 first-boot RAM overlay fallback the ERR line looked like a real
failure in the boot log.

Only run the copy when /tmp/root/upper exists.

Signed-off-by: e2631 tree fork <e2631@localhost>

diff --git a/libfstools/overlay.c b/libfstools/overlay.c
index ce17a99..b37d4dc 100644
--- a/libfstools/overlay.c
+++ b/libfstools/overlay.c
@@ -344,7 +344,9 @@ jffs2_switch(struct volume *v)
 
 		/* try hard to be in sync */
 		ULOG_INFO("synchronizing overlay\n");
-		if (system("cp -a /tmp/root/upper/* / 2>/dev/null"))
+		/* a first boot with a RAM overlay has no jffs2 upper yet */
+		if (access("/tmp/root/upper", F_OK) == 0 &&
+		    system("cp -a /tmp/root/upper/* / 2>/dev/null"))
 			ULOG_ERR("failed to sync jffs2 overlay\n");
 		break;
 
